# CML direction from Dr Bujok

When a concrete plan is given without a request for suggestions, execute it exactly. Do not offer alternative layouts, colors, or copy “improvements.”

## MONOTASK (agents)

- One coherent task at a time. Finish it. Do not parallelize redesigns, “while we’re here” polish, or sleep-talk alternatives.
- When ready files / HTML / assets are handed over: **copy-paste and adapt** — do not regenerate or reinvent UI from scratch.
- Source of truth for CML start: `refs/bmcml/BMCML-offline.html` (from Downloads `BMCML-offline (2).html`). Assets: `public/cml/start-gabinet.png`, `public/brand/logo-bujok-medical.png`.

## First screen (locked visual)

- Full-bleed rocky gabinet photo is the calm start of the conversation.
- Warm **yellow** waterfall stays the light center.
- Green tree on the left stays as the living accent.
- Everything else stays darkened for private, intimate talk.
- Never apply `hue-rotate` or a green cast over the whole hero photo.
- Text sits at the **bottom** (thumb zone); the upper field stays open for the image.

